# Routines whose bodies are hand-written rather than generated. apple2tc emits
# a declaration for each and rewrites every call site to it; the definitions
# live in a2rom.c and game.c, stitched into one translation unit by
# snake-byte-ext.c.
#
# The file is still called rom.externs for history's sake -- it began as ROM
# entry points only. It now also carries game routines, which is the point of
# the exercise: every line moved from the second list to a readable definition
# is a piece of Snake Byte that no longer looks like a decompiler's output.
#
# apple2tc takes a single --extern-routines= path, so both lists share a file.

# Apple II ROM entry points -- a2rom.c
F800 rom_plot
F819 rom_hline
F864 rom_setcol
F871 rom_scrn
FC58 rom_home
FC68 rom_fc68
FDED rom_cout
FE89 rom_setkbd
FE93 rom_setvid

# Snake Byte's own routines -- game.c
6127 game_load_shape
60E7 game_draw_cell
60E4 game_plot_shape
